<title>USA: Northern States shuts King coal power unit.</title>
<headline>Northern States shuts King coal power unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern States Power Co has shut its 581 megawatt Allen King coal-fired power plant for repairs, but the unit should return to service early Sunday morning, a company spokeswoman said Friday.</p>
<p>The unit was shut Friday to repair a boiler tube leak, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The King plant is located in Oak Parks Heights near Stillwater, Minn., and came on line in 1968.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
